# Secret-scan rules and allowlist (T832, T833): the single source read by both
# tui/tests/secret_scan.rs (every tracked file, under cargo test) and
# scripts/hooks/pre-commit (each staged file, as staged), so the two cannot
# drift. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Fields are
# separated by one TAB.
#
#   rule<TAB>name<TAB>accept<TAB>before<TAB>secret<TAB>after
#
# name is what a failure reports. secret is the credential's shape, written so
# it means the same as a POSIX extended regular expression (grep -E) and as a
# Rust regex (the regex crate): only literals, bracket expressions, ( | ),
# ?, *, + and {m,n}; no \d, no (?:...), no backslash escapes. before and
# after are one bracket expression each, or "-" for none: the match must
# start at the start of a line or after a character of before, and end at
# the end of a line or before a character of after, so a secret never starts
# or ends inside a longer word. accept is "any", or "random": the part after
# the secret's first "-" must hold both a digit and a letter, as a random key
# does and a long kebab-case word does not.
#
# The shapes are spelled so this file never matches itself (a header with
# -{5} instead of five dashes, AKI[A] instead of the literal prefix).
#
#   allow<TAB>path<TAB>reason
#
# A repository-relative file that may deliberately hold a secret-shaped fake,
# with the reason. cargo test fails on an allow line whose file no longer
# matches, so the list cannot go stale. There is none today: the fakes the
# tests use (sk-ant-test, sk-ant-abc, TOKEN=secret) are too short to match.

rule	private key	any	-	-{5}BEGIN ([A-Z0-9]+ )*PRIVATE KEY( BLOCK)?-{5}	-
rule	AWS access key id	any	[^A-Z0-9]	AKI[A][0-9A-Z]{16}	[^A-Z0-9]
rule	GitHub token	any	[^A-Za-z0-9_]	gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}|github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{82}	[^A-Za-z0-9_]
rule	Slack token	any	[^A-Za-z0-9]	xox[baprs]-[0-9]{6,}-[0-9A-Za-z-]{8,}	-
rule	Anthropic API key	any	[^A-Za-z0-9_-]	sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,}	-
rule	OpenAI-style API key	random	[^A-Za-z0-9_-]	sk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{40,}	-
